\begin{corollary} \label{maincordim2}
Let $g$ be a Riemannian metric on $\T^2$ and let $g_0$ its normalized conformally equivalent flat metric. Then, $\beta_g(h) \leq \beta_{g_0}(h)$ for every $h\in H_1(\T^2;\R)$. Moreover, equality holds at some  $h\in H_1(\T^2;\R)\setminus \{0\}$ if and only if $g = g_0$, i.e., $g$ is flat.
